    fix(daemon): guard DF-024 output accounting behind detector existence
    
    this.convergence is constructed in start() after config.load(); a directly
    constructed Daemon (OBS-3 daemon-prom tests, embedders) has no detector, so
    the unconditional reportPipelineOutputs call crashed every pipeline with
    'reading recordOutputs of null' and turned successes into pipeline errors.
    Skip accounting when the detector is absent (pre-024 behavior); started
    daemons keep full input/output accounting.
    
    Full suite: 129 files / 2095 tests green; build clean. Regression introduced
    by the harvested DF-024 WIP baseline (06a98f87); caught by the README-CLUSTER-R3
    tier1 judge and attributed against base 94e2b921 (daemon-prom tests green there).
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
---
 specs/daemon.spec.dir/src/daemon.ts | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/specs/daemon.spec.dir/src/daemon.ts b/specs/daemon.spec.dir/src/daemon.ts
index 3ba2039e..1e5e8917 100644
--- a/specs/daemon.spec.dir/src/daemon.ts
+++ b/specs/daemon.spec.dir/src/daemon.ts
@@ -436,7 +436,14 @@ export class Daemon extends EventEmitter {
         throw error;
       }
 
-      this.reportPipelineOutputs(beforeOutputs, pipelineResult?.success === true);
+      // DF-SPECLANG-024: attribute what this convergence pass WROTE — but only
+      // when the detector exists. this.convergence is constructed in start()
+      // (after config.load()), so a directly-constructed Daemon (tests, embedders)
+      // has no detector; skipping accounting there matches the pre-024 behavior
+      // instead of crashing every pipeline on "reading 'recordOutputs' of null".
+      if (this.convergence) {
+        this.reportPipelineOutputs(beforeOutputs, pipelineResult?.success === true);
+      }
 
       if (pipelineResult.success) {
         this.pipelineFailures = 0;
